      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143471",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}, X_{4}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cB(5, \u03b8)$ with unknown probability of success $\u03b8$. You're given the particular sample\n$x_{1} = 5, x_{2} = 3, x_{3} = 2, x_{4} = 1$.\nThe log-likelihood function of the sample is given by\n$l(\u03b8) = \\ln a + b\\ln \u03b8 + c\\ln (1 - \u03b8)$.\n\nFind the value of $a + b + c$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
